<report>
<title>Unpaired t test</title>

<p>Mean of @title_0 = @{mean_0:roundu}  (n = @n0)<br />
Mean of @title_1 = @{mean_1:roundu}  (n = @n1)</p>

<p><u>Assuming equal variances</u><br />
Combined standard error = @{error:roundu}<br />
df = @df<br />
t =  @{t:roundu}<br />
<pval>One sided @{p_1:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2:pval}</pval></p>

<p><ci>@{pc:round2}% confidence interval for difference between means = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>Power @pwr</p>

<p><u>Assuming unequal variances</u><br />
Combined standard error = @{error_unequal:roundu}<br />
df = @{df_unequal:roundu}<br />
t(d) =  @{t_unequal:roundu}<br />
<pval>One sided @{p_1_unequal:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2_unequal:pval}</pval></p>

<p><ci>@{pc_unequal:round2}% confidence interval for difference between means = @{from_unequal:roundu} to @{to_unequal:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>Power @pwr_unequal</p>

<p><u>Comparison of variances</u><br />
@say1<br />
@say2</p>
</report>
